Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-24-2001||10:17 AM||||This guy keeps repeadly "attacking" or flooding me and it's getting annoying (I am left without the itnernet for about 20 minutes). I looked where it was coming from, and it was Africa, but this guy is american, and I guarantee thats not his real ISP. Anyways, I tried this one program called ZoneAttack or something, but it just registered the attack over and over until I crashed. I want to try that black ice again, but I fear it will do the same thing? Some guys are saying he has "The bandwidth of a small nation" and if I try to take any action against him, they're words were "Do you honestly think you'll ever be able to use the internet again?" but there HAS to be a good program to defend from such attacks! My problem with blackice, is that I already ran the evaluation one awhile ago, and whenver I install it, it says eval period ended. I searched teh registry and deleted everything inthere, but the same thign. You guys have an idea of how to make it work again? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mblackwell||04-24-2001||07:56 PM||||Maybe you could ask your ISP for a new IP address.||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||04-24-2001||09:05 PM||||Are you sure he attacking YOU and not just sweeping IP's looking for open ports in random computers? it might come up as him wicked attacking you but really he is just scanning you ports and black ice may come up with a waring every port he scans<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||04-24-2001||09:17 PM||||ZoneAlarm is free for personal use @  <A HREF="http://www.zonelabs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zonelabs.com</A> .  It is pretty powerful and easy to install.  Try that and see if it does not solve your problems.  <P>Also, if you have cable or DSL modem from an ISP that provides "dynamic" IP addressing, you might try clicking on <B>Start</B> then <B>Run</B> then typing <B>Winipcfg</B>.  When the box pops up you will see your IP address.  Click on <B>Release All</B> then click <B>Renew All</B>.  That should pull a new IP address for you and hopefully give you some relief.  <P>Definitely install some sort of firewall.  As I said, ZoneAlarm is free for personal use, but if you dont like that one you should definitely invest in one of the others available for minimal cost.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||04-24-2001||11:15 PM||||Download Neotrace and it will give you the guys internet provider and should be able to even give you his name, address, and city he is in. The program is real slick, after you plugin the guys IP address it will give you the email addresses for his provider to launch a complaint. I have managed to bust several university students using this program who are trying to get into my machine. Grab it from<BR> <A HREF="http://www.neotrace.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.neotrace.com/</A> <P>If you need any help with it, drop me a line at loafer@sk.sympatico.ca<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||85Josh||04-25-2001||12:20 AM||||Definatly try ZoneAlarm,set it to high security and he won't even be able to see your computer. <P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
