Z||000011||Mach10||04-28-2001||07:42 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Some guys are saying he has "The bandwidth of a small nation" and if I try to take any action against him, they're words were "Do you honestly think you'll ever be able to use the internet again?"<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Baloney. Take him to the cleaners. If the "small nation" finds out who's using their bandwidth, do you think that HE/SHE'll ever be using the net again? The FBI takes great interest in people that bounce internationally and commit data crimes.<BR>Take him/her to the cleaners.<BR>Find the ISP that he's using (or bouncing from) and call his ass in.<BR>I HATE SCRIPT KIDDIES!<BR>They make my work miserable.<P>Oh, and Loafer; I use  <A HREF="http://www.visualroute.com" TARGET=_blank>www.visualroute.com</A>  <BR>It's faster, cos I don;t need to download, and whoever it is won't see me coming, as it's Visual route that's fingering him...<BR>BTW, you won't be able to get any personal info on the person unless he's dumb enough to set up a finger server on his box. That said, university students usually automatically have their info on the U's finger server, hence the info you can harvest. Don't assume that the IP you see is the one that's attacking you. I know people that have been set up to take the fall like that, because people don't understand the concept of IP/MAC spoofing.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 04-28-2001).]||||reg||1
